            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Influence and Legacy</strong><br>\nDiogenes' philosophy influenced not just his contemporaries but also many who came after him. His legacy is found in the works of later philosophers, particularly the Stoics, who admired his strength in enduring hardship and his determination to live by his principles.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Anecdotes and Teachings</strong><br>\nDiogenes' teachings were passed down through anecdotes, which showcase his sharp wit and his method of teaching through living. He often performed outrageous acts to illustrate his points, like publicly mocking the folly of extravagant lifestyles and pretentious behavior.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Remembrance</strong><br>\nDiogenes died at the age of approximately 89 in Corinth. Though he left no written works, his legacy persisted through stories and accounts by others. Even today, Diogenes is remembered as a figure who challenged the social order and emphasized a life of authenticity over one of material wealth.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
